  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Preheat oven to 220°C/200°C fan-forced. <br>• Finely chop brown onion. Finely chop or crush garlic. Rinse red lentils. <br>• Grate carrot. Roughly chop tomato.<br>• Cut the haloumi into bite-sized chunks.</p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/697ad791bcdfd65d69c381b6/step-63d50d00.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• <p>• In a large saucepan, melt the butter and a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat. <br>• Cook onion, carrot and tomato until softened, 3-4 mins. Add garlic, masala spice blend, mild curry paste and tomato paste and cook until fragrant, 1-2 mins. <br>• Add the water, lentils and coconut milk. Stir to combine. Cover with lid, reduce heat to medium and simmer until lentils are softened, 20-25 mins (add a splash of water if the dhal looks dry).</p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/697ad791bcdfd65d69c381b6/step-f6199510.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Cut mini flour tortillas into 2cm strips. Divide tortillas between the lined oven trays. Brush (or spray) with olive oil and season with salt and pepper. <br>• Bake until lightly golden and crisp, 8-10 mins. <br>• In a large frying pan, heat a generous drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat. <br>• When oil is hot, cook haloumi, tossing occasionally, until golden brown, 2-4 mins. </p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/697ad791bcdfd65d69c381b6/step-0a804520.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Divide dhal between bowls.  Stir through cooked haloumi. Top with Greek-style yoghurt. Serve with flatbread dippers.</p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/697ad791bcdfd65d69c381b6/step-97ee9730.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
